WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.3 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Indicators

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
An indicator is a clear sign that a result is happening, measured the same way by everyone.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.504
An indicator is a specific sign you track to show whether a result is happening. It is defined so clearly that you, a co-founder or the first person who joins would all measure it the same way.

4
00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:29.504
What every indicator records

5
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:41.574
Definition: The sign you track, with who counts as a success and out of whom. For example: % of tutoring pupils who pass their maths exam, out of all who finished.

6
00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:50.681
Source and method: Where the data comes from and how you collect it. For example: The results slip a parent shows at the final session.

7
00:00:50.681 --> 00:00:56.826
Frequency: How often you collect it. For example: Once a term, two weeks after exams.

8
00:00:56.826 --> 00:01:04.911
Owner: Who collects it and answers for it. For example: The founder, until a second tutor joins.

9
00:01:05.311 --> 00:01:05.911
Why it matters

10
00:01:05.911 --> 00:01:11.215
1. It turns a vague hope into something you can check.

11
00:01:11.215 --> 00:01:16.519
2. Everyone measures the same way, so numbers compare over time.

12
00:01:16.519 --> 00:01:22.822
3. Breaking data down shows unequal results from your first group.

13
00:01:23.222 --> 00:01:23.822
What it guides

14
00:01:23.822 --> 00:01:28.756
1. Your baselines and targets, set in the next lesson.

15
00:01:28.756 --> 00:01:34.430
2. Your data collection plan: each indicator needs a source and method.

16
00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:40.363
3. Your monitoring dashboard: planned versus actual for each indicator.

17
00:01:40.763 --> 00:01:41.363
What to avoid

18
00:01:41.363 --> 00:01:45.556
Counting activities, like sessions run, as outcomes.

19
00:01:45.556 --> 00:01:49.748
Percentages without a clear numerator and denominator.

20
00:01:49.748 --> 00:01:56.422
Counting the same person twice, or data you cannot collect ethically.

21
00:01:57.022 --> 00:01:58.822
You write an indicator reference sheet for your priority results.

22
00:01:58.822 --> 00:02:02.822
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:04.322 --> 00:02:07.422
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
